## Class Notes:
- Active buzzer: produces sound when connected to power, has a built-in oscillator and fixed pitch
- Passive buzzer: needs an external signal to produce sound, different frequencies can be used to play differnet notes
- Ultrasonic distance sensor: uses sound waves to measure the distamce to an object through sending out signals and measuring the time until the echo returns
- Similar sensors: infrared sensor and PIR(passive infrared) sensorwhich detects thermal radiation (heat) from moving bodies 
- Push button: a digital input that changes its state when pressed

